+| F11-DCR7 | D-CR7 ledger-date policy for stock movements | **For this release: keep the current behaviour.** `stock_movements` carries only the posting time `createdAt`; a warehouse document's business date (`warehouse_transactions.movementDate`) stays on the document and is not carried to the ledger; the Warehouse Movements report filters by posting time. Any change (labelling the report "posting date", or carrying the business date onto the ledger with a migration and backfill) needs the authorised owner's approval. | ACCOUNTING_POLICY_OWNER; INVENTORY_OWNER | F11_COMPLETION_REPORT.md §4 M-2; inventory-movement-dates spec test 3 (pins the policy) | any change of the ledger-date basis | RECORDED (current behaviour retained for this release) |
+| F11-TZ | Target-host database session time zone | Run, read-only, on the target host's database as the application role: `SHOW timezone;` and `SELECT now(), current_date;` and attach the output. The movement-report day boundaries (and the existing `dateFrom`, sub-ledger `entryDate` filters) use this zone; local and test clusters are `Africa/Cairo`; the application sets no session zone of its own. | ENVIRONMENT_OWNER; READ_ONLY_OPERATOR | F11_COMPLETION_REPORT.md §4, §7 | confirmation of the M-1 boundary on the host | PENDING (no host access) |
+| F11-RFQ | RFQ-award dead-letter for an item discontinued after PR approval | Retained as a documented residual risk; no rebuild in this scope. The award PO is created by the outbox handler; a refused create is retried and then marked `failed`, the RFQ stays `sent` with no PO (same mechanism already applied to draft items). A buyer-visible exception is a separate future scope. | CTO | F11_COMPLETION_REPORT.md §7 | — | RECORDED (residual risk) |
